      <title>How poisonous mercury can get from coal-fired power plants into fish you eat — EPA just weakened rules meant to lower the risk</title>
      <link>https://www.downtoearth.org.in/energy/how-poisonous-mercury-can-get-from-coal-fired-power-plants-into-fish-you-eat-epa-just-weakened-rules-meant-to-lower-the-risk</link>
      <description>The EPA has weakened mercury emission rules for coal plants, raising concerns about increased mercury in fish. This rollback could heighten health risks, especially for children and pregnant women, as mercury bioaccumulates in the food chain, impacting brain development and public health costs.</description>
