      <title>Killer beetles in the baobabs: Researcher warns of risk to African trees</title>
      <link>https://www.downtoearth.org.in/africa/killer-beetles-in-the-baobabs-researcher-warns-of-risk-to-african-trees</link>
      <description>Baobab trees face a new threat from the mango stem-borer beetle, which has killed several trees in Oman. Researchers warn that if the beetle spreads to Africa, it could devastate ecosystems and livelihoods. Early detection and biological control are crucial to prevent its spread.</description>
